Title: Treat the AmigaDOS volume colon as a path boundary
Repository: libresprite
Base: 89ea7597ed1d779e85c0019555f5b97c7eac22f0
Requires: preceding patches in series
Date: 2026-11-16
Author: aros-libresprite project
Problem: AmigaDOS paths start with a volume or assign name and a colon ("Work:Art/pic.png", "RAM:pic.png"). The path helpers only knew '/' and '\\', so "RAM:pic.png" had no directory and join_path("RAM:", "x") gave "RAM:/x", which means the parent of RAM:.
Change: On AROS the colon also ends a path component; get_file_path keeps it ("RAM:"), join_path adds no '/' after it.
Scope: AROS
Upstream: candidate
Verification: Built for mainline AROS x86_64 (GCC 10.5, SDK nightly 20261110); LibreSprite starts on nightly 20261113 (pool v1-1, 2026-11-16)
Removal: None planned.
---
diff --git a/src/base/path.cpp b/src/base/path.cpp
index 478434da4894b2c4feb73ef711a78605de9afacf..271a050798324e0b75b696bfcdf11c59f0c5810f 100644
--- a/src/base/path.cpp
+++ b/src/base/path.cpp
@@ -32,16 +32,30 @@ bool is_path_separator(std::string::value_type chr)
   return (chr == '\\' || chr == '/');
 }
 
+// Where the last path component starts. On AROS the colon after a volume or
+// assign name ("Work:", "RAM:") also ends a path component.
+static bool is_component_boundary(std::string::value_type chr)
+{
+#ifdef __AROS__
+  return is_path_separator(chr) || chr == ':';
+#else
+  return is_path_separator(chr);
+#endif
+}
+
 std::string get_file_path(const std::string& filename)
 {
   std::string::const_reverse_iterator rit;
   std::string res;
 
   for (rit=filename.rbegin(); rit!=filename.rend(); ++rit)
-    if (is_path_separator(*rit))
+    if (is_component_boundary(*rit))
       break;
 
   if (rit != filename.rend()) {
+    // "Work:file" lives in "Work:", not in "Work".
+    if (!is_path_separator(*rit))
+      --rit;
     ++rit;
     std::copy(filename.begin(), std::string::const_iterator(rit.base()),
               std::back_inserter(res));
